  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member browsing a forum list, I want \"Page N\" without an invented total whenever HFR does not give the real page count, so that the app never shows a fake last page.\n\n### Scope\n\nAdd the exactness flag to `PageNavigation` (HFRModels): whether the page count is exact (a real `sujetCase4` count or pager total) or only a lower bound. The parser (LOT-022) sets it and the app (app lists) disables \"Dernière page\" when it is false. Engine side only; the exact per-row page count of topics is kept.\n\n- Module: HFRModels · Difficulty: easy · Priority: high\n- Implements: FEAT-003 (#147), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md); related bug #104; LOT-082 (#100, merged) already shows no fake total\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): none, new behaviour (HFR-PROTOCOL §7b B1)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-167-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- none (LOT-010 (#43, done) defines `PageNavigation`)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `PageNavigation` carries the flag, `Codable` backward compatible; Swift Testing tests shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-167-*.md` written; FEAT-003 spec created when the lot starts (ADR 0011 §2).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n",
